# BRIDGE PATCH -- not a local customisation, and not a fork of grading behaviour.
#
# WHAT GAP. `gradeOneVector` grades content-digest vectors against the agent's declared
# profile when it is given one (`agentCapability`, or the narrower
# `agentContentDigestPolicy`). The storyboard dispatch never gives it either.
# `probe-dispatch.ts` DOES read `_profile.raw_capabilities.request_signing` -- in
# `declaredProtocolMethodCoverage` -- but takes only `protocol_methods_required_for` from
# it for the vector-028 gate. `covers_content_digest` sits unread in the same block, and no
# `--signing-*` CLI flag exposes it either.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS. `negative/007-missing-content-digest` asserts a verifier declaring
# `covers_content_digest: 'required'` and `negative/018-digest-covered-when-forbidden`
# asserts `'forbidden'`. An agent declares exactly ONE value, so a run that grades both has
# at least one guaranteed failure whatever the agent implements. When this patch was
# written this seller declared `'either'`, so it answered 200 to both and failed both.
# Measured then: run innet_210926_0617 scored 101/17 on each protocol against 101/15 on the
# pinned build, and the two extra failures were exactly 007 and 018 on both cards.
#
# THAT PREMISE NO LONGER HOLDS, AND THE SCOPE PARAGRAPH BELOW IS MEASURED AGAINST IT.
# At the 3.2.1 pin this seller declares `covers_content_digest: 'required'`, not `'either'`:
# `get-adcp-capabilities-response.json`'s allOf if/then makes it `{"const": "required"}`
# once `request_signing.supported` is true, and `_validate_digest_coverage`
# (src/core/schemas/capability_declarations.py) refuses anything else. So `'either'` is no
# longer available to go back to, and the two-unanswerable-vectors problem this patch was
# built for is now ONE vector: at `'required'`, upstream's `contentDigestDeclarationMismatch`
# skips 018 on the declaration alone and 007 becomes answerable (our verifier returns
# `request_signature_components_incomplete`, which is what 007 expects).
#
# WHAT THAT COSTS NOW. `contentDigestStructuralMismatch` -- the OTHER predicate the same
# input reaches -- skips every vector whose `Signature-Input` does not cover content-digest,
# on the stated grounds that "the verifier rejects with
# `request_signature_components_incomplete` before the vector's intended error path can
# fire". That premise is false for the verifier this repo runs: `verify_request_signature`
# calls `_check_params_present` (step 2), `_check_tag` (3), `_check_alg` (4), `_check_window`
# (5) and only THEN `_check_components` (6, where the digest policy lives) --
# adcp/signing/verifier.py:320-336, sequential, first failure raised. A vector whose intended
# error is at step 1-5 therefore DOES reach its intended error path. Measured on run
# innet_091026_1343: 19 signed_requests checks that passed at the 3.1.1 pin now skip
# `capability_profile_mismatch`, and nine of them -- negative 002 (tag, step 3), 003 (expired,
# 5), 004 (window, 5), 005 (alg, 4), 006 (@authority, 6 but raised by the REQUIRED_COMPONENTS
# loop ahead of the policy check, same error code), 012 (expires param, 2), 013
# (expires<=created, 5), 014 (nonce param, 2), 022 (multi-valued content-type, 1) -- assert
# an error this verifier returns before the policy check runs. The other ten are correctly
# skipped: three positives genuinely cannot verify without digest coverage under
# `'required'`, 008/009/015/016/017/020 assert errors at steps 7-12 that the step-6 refusal
# really does pre-empt, and 026 is independently `transport_ungradable`.
#
# NOT FIXED HERE, DELIBERATELY. Narrowing the structural predicate to respect the verifier
# checklist order is a change to upstream GRADING logic, which is exactly what the SCOPE
# paragraph promises this patch does not do, and it cannot be graded without the storyboard
# leg. It belongs upstream alongside #2993. Dropping this patch instead is NOT the answer:
# with no policy forwarded, `preflightSkip` reaches neither predicate (both arms are gated on
# `agentCapability || agentContentDigestPolicy`), so 018 would come back as a graded FAILURE.
#
# UPSTREAM. Filed as adcontextprotocol/adcp-client#2993, with the suggested derivation.
# This is the storyboard-side half of #2963: that PR's grader-side half merged and works --
# `contentDigestDeclarationMismatch` and `CONTENT_DIGEST_POLICY_REFUSALS` are present in
# rc.42 and correctly narrow the skip to those two vectors -- but nothing reaches them from
# the storyboard path. So this bridge supplies the ONE missing input, and relies on
# upstream's own predicate to decide what to do with it.
#
# SCOPE. One module, in its CJS and ESM builds: read the declared policy off the profile
# already in hand and forward it as `agentContentDigestPolicy`. It adds no grading rule, no
# skip logic and no vector list. `agentContentDigestPolicy` rather than the full
# `agentCapability` fixture is deliberate -- the protocol-method half of the profile is
# already handled upstream, and the policy alone skips exactly 007 and 018 while
# `positive/002`, `negative/010` and `negative/023` keep grading.
#
# NOTHING ELSE FROM THE RETIRED rc.35 PATCH COMES BACK. In particular the
# `legacyCompat: { enabled: false }` flip must NOT be reinstated in any form: measured, on
# current main `true` is the card-following setting, and `false` silently sends 1.0 framing
# to an agent that published 0.3.
#
# DELETE THIS WHEN adcontextprotocol/adcp-client#2993 lands and the runner pin moves to a
# release containing it -- i.e. when the storyboard dispatch derives the policy itself.
# The check that it is safe to delete was "with the patch removed, `signed_requests` still
# reports zero failures on both protocols, and 007/018 come back as `not_selected` /
# `profile_excluded` rather than as graded failures". That check was written against the
# `'either'` declaration and no longer decides anything: at `'required'` the skip arms are
# gated on this patch's own input, so removing it regrades 018 as a failure and the check
# can never pass. Re-derive it against whatever upstream lands, rather than running it.
#
diff --git a/node_modules/@adcp/sdk/dist/lib/testing/storyboard/request-signing/probe-dispatch.js b/node_modules/@adcp/sdk/dist/lib/testing/storyboard/request-signing/probe-dispatch.js
